From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:40:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 156/207] runner: Session.destroy joins every translation
 before freeing any cell

A cell's translation borrows earlier notebook cells' code as its prior (no copy). destroy joined
and freed cells in order, so a later cell's translator still running at teardown could read an
earlier cell's freed code. Length-cap (a fence closing on the final token with can_hold false)
and cancel (taken before the runner tick) both reach destroy with that translator pending
(S1's finding, T5's gdb reproduction). The test forces that interleaving: the later translator
watches its prior while destroy runs and must never see it freed.
---
 zig/src/core/runner.zig               |  3 +-
 zig/src/core/runner_teardown_test.zig | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 zig/src/core/runner_test.zig          |  1 +
 3 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 zig/src/core/runner_teardown_test.zig

